<title>CANADA: Ontario sets C$500 million bond due June, 2027.</title>
<headline>Ontario sets C$500 million bond due June, 2027.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Province of Ontario on Wednesday set C$500 million of 7.6 percent bonds due June 2, 2027 in financial markets, said lead manager Nesbitt Burns.</p>
<p>The bond was priced at C$101.607 to yield 7.46 percent, 24 basis points over the Government of Canada's 8.0 percent bond due June 1, 2023.</p>
<p>The issue, which settles on April 3, 1997, will pay its first coupon on June 2, 1997.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
